        "id": "1890",
        "question": "The diagram shows an equilateral triangle RST and also the triangle $T U V$ obtained by rotating triangle $R S T$ about the point $T$. Angle $R T V=70^{\\circ}$. What is angle $R S V$ ? <image1>",
        "options": [
          "$20^{\\circ}$",
          "$25^{\\circ}$",
          "$30^{\\circ}$",
          "$35^{\\circ}$",
          "$40^{\\circ}$"
        ],
        "image": "images/1890.jpg",
        "decoded_image": {
          "path": "images/1890.jpg",
          "original_path": "1890.jpg"
        },
        "answer": "D",
        "solution": "Since triangle $S T R$ is equilateral, $\\angle S T R=60^{\\circ}$. Hence $\\angle S T V=130^{\\circ}$. Triangle $S T V$ is isosceles (since $S T=T V$ ), so $\\angle T S V=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(180^{\\circ}-130^{\\circ}\\right)=25^{\\circ}$. Thus $\\angle R S V=60^{\\circ}-25^{\\circ}=35^{\\circ}$.",
        "level": 4,
        "subject": "transformation geometry"
      },
      "source_package": "MathVision_redrawn_transformation_geometry_160_final",
